    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1189">

                <pb facs="1389" n="1191" xml:id="pg1191"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.79641/8–2145: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 1189<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of
                            State to the Chief of the Aviation Division</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morgan</hi>)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1189-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-08-21T18:00:00-04:00">August 21, 1945—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7101. For Stokeley Morgan.</p>
                <p>Potsdam meeting did not go into aviation questions except for statement from
                    Secretary to Cadogan that discussion of
                    problem was desired.…<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1189-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Byrnes</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        J[ohn] B[ell]
                    </signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1189-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d1189-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to the American Embassy, London.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1189-f2" n="2" xml:id="d1189-f2-content">
                <p>No other papers relating to this Byrnes–Cadogan
                    conversation have been found. Concerning a Truman–Churchill
                    conversation on this subject, however, see <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>,
                        <ref target="#pg80">p. 80</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
